{
  "case_id": "2009-08-1555",
  "document_hash": "22ceb54e65f01626776cfb7f0ecf6bd9e1b8af1edc60c36d44eb3ba7be4bcf84",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1555",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ceb54e65f01626776cfb7f0ecf6bd9e1b8af1edc60c36d44eb3ba7be4bcf84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ceb54e65f0-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Shay Dvoretzky (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1555",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ceb54e65f01626776cfb7f0ecf6bd9e1b8af1edc60c36d44eb3ba7be4bcf84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ceb54e65f0-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The FSIA applies to suits against foreign officials for acts taken on the state's behalf, because such suits are the equivalent of a suit against the state directly."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1555",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ceb54e65f01626776cfb7f0ecf6bd9e1b8af1edc60c36d44eb3ba7be4bcf84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ceb54e65f0-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What -- what authority do you have for that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Shay Dvoretzky",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1555",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ceb54e65f01626776cfb7f0ecf6bd9e1b8af1edc60c36d44eb3ba7be4bcf84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ceb54e65f0-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Torture Victim Protection Act creates a cause of action but is silent about immunity, and, therefore, has to be interpreted consistently with background immunity principles and consistently with a preexisting statute codifying immunity, rather than --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1555",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ceb54e65f01626776cfb7f0ecf6bd9e1b8af1edc60c36d44eb3ba7be4bcf84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ceb54e65f0-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there -- is there any Alien Tort Statute or the torture statute that would have survived, under your view, because your view is it's no exception under the Foreign Sovereign Immunities Act, end of case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1555",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ceb54e65f01626776cfb7f0ecf6bd9e1b8af1edc60c36d44eb3ba7be4bcf84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ceb54e65f0-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: And there was no uncertainty about -- about individuals?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1555",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ceb54e65f01626776cfb7f0ecf6bd9e1b8af1edc60c36d44eb3ba7be4bcf84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ceb54e65f0-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: So they didn't have to say yes, but if they said no, that -- it pretty much carried the day?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Millett",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1555",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ceb54e65f01626776cfb7f0ecf6bd9e1b8af1edc60c36d44eb3ba7be4bcf84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ceb54e65f0-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MILLETT: It doesn't seem strange, for precisely the reason that we have still with us today a former minister of defense when we have no Ministry of Defense and no Government of Somalia whatsoever."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1555",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "22ceb54e65f01626776cfb7f0ecf6bd9e1b8af1edc60c36d44eb3ba7be4bcf84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ceb54e65f0-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the State Department didn't show up for 2 years."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1555",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "22ceb54e65f01626776cfb7f0ecf6bd9e1b8af1edc60c36d44eb3ba7be4bcf84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ceb54e65f0-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, do you agree with the Solicitor General's position about the preservation of the immunities that existed before?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Executive Branch",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1555",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "22ceb54e65f01626776cfb7f0ecf6bd9e1b8af1edc60c36d44eb3ba7be4bcf84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ceb54e65f0-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Executive Branch decides. We tell the court. And if we don't tell the court that this person can be sued, then the person can't be sued."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Shay Dvoretzky)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1555",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ceb54e65f01626776cfb7f0ecf6bd9e1b8af1edc60c36d44eb3ba7be4bcf84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ceb54e65f0-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DVORETZKY: First of all, as we argue in our brief, this has not historically been a long-standing power of the Executive in the way that the immunity itself has been recognized under the common law. And what Congress did in 1976 was it codified the substance of the common law but took away that procedure."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1555",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ceb54e65f01626776cfb7f0ecf6bd9e1b8af1edc60c36d44eb3ba7be4bcf84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ceb54e65f0-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: How does this case --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1555",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ceb54e65f01626776cfb7f0ecf6bd9e1b8af1edc60c36d44eb3ba7be4bcf84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ceb54e65f0-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask just ask one quick question? Am I correct in understanding that you do not contend that your client was covered by 1603(b)(1)?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1555",
      "confidence": 0.0,
